{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-10-29T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"What stories could these walls tell? Rising above eastern Bohemia in Czechia, Kunětická hora Castle has witnessed centuries of history. Dating to the late 14th century, the castle gradually evolved into an impressive fortress and noble residence. Its elevated position offered commanding views of the surrounding countryside and helped make it an important stronghold.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-CA2792060952_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.KuneticeCastle_EN-CA2792060952_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where history stands watch","Title":"Kunětická hora Castle, Bohemia, Czechia","Copyright":"© Marek Saroch/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.080287,15.811615/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.080287,15.811615;S9;Kunětická hora Castle, Czechia&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Kun%c4%9btick%c3%a1+hora+Castle&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261028_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261028_KuneticeCastle"},"Ssd":"20261028","Name":"KuneticeCastle","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2792060952","FullDateString":"Oct 28, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in calm water and glowing in the light of the setting sun, this grove of pond cypress creates a striking display of colour and symmetry. Native to the southeastern United States, the species is associated with shallow ponds, depressions and wetland habitats. This image was captured in Georgia, where these trees can be found in places such as the Okefenokee Swamp and other low-lying wetlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-CA4795569261_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PondCypress_EN-CA4795569261_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's golden mirror","Title":"A grove of pond cypress trees with fall foliage, Georgia, United States","Copyright":"© Chris Moore/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Pond cypress can develop knobby root structures known as 'knees' that rise above the water or soil around the tree.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Pond+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261027_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261027_PondCypress"},"Ssd":"20261027","Name":"PondCypress","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4795569261","FullDateString":"Oct 27, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Bulgaria's Western Rhodope Mountains, autumn leaves gather beside the rushing waters of Sitovo Waterfall. Near the village of Sitovo, southwest of Plovdiv, the falls tumble beneath an old stone bridge whose arch frames the cascades like a storybook scene. Moss-covered stones and pine trees add shades of green to the autumn landscape, while fallen leaves gather along the water's edge or drift through its pools. The falls become especially lively after rain and during spring snowmelt, when the surrounding woodland echoes with the sound of rushing water.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-CA2117878012_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SitovoWaterfall_EN-CA2117878012_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Nature's fall soundtrack","Title":"Autumn waterfalls near Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria","Copyright":"© Nadya85/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.926863,24.615841/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.926863,24.615841;S9;Sitovo, Plovdiv Province, Bulgaria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sitovo+Plovdiv+Bulgaria&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261026_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261026_SitovoWaterfall"},"Ssd":"20261026","Name":"SitovoWaterfall","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"2117878012","FullDateString":"Oct 26, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some mountains make you work for the view. Mount Sneffels makes you work for the last few hundred metres. Rising to 4,310 metres in Colorado's San Juan Mountains, this fourteener is a familiar sight around Ridgway, Ouray and Telluride. It sits within the 67-square-kilometre Mount Sneffels Wilderness, a protected area designated in 1980. Hikers can reach the mountain from several approaches, including the Yankee Boy Basin and the Blue Lakes area.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_EN-CA1700205921_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SneffelsAutumn_EN-CA1700205921_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"'Peak' into Colorado","Title":"Mount Sneffels in the San Juan Mountains near Ridgway, Colorado, United States","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/38.00354,-107.792695/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=38.00354,-107.792695;S9;Mount Sneffels, Colorado, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261025_SneffelsAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Mount+Sneffels&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261025_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261025_SneffelsAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261025","Name":"SneffelsAutumn","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"1700205921","FullDateString":"Oct 25, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're inside the Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, where the humble act of opening a book took on grand architectural ambitions. Founded in 1837 by 43 Portuguese immigrants, just 15 years after Brazil's independence, the institution eventually moved into the building seen here, completed half a century later in a lavish Neo-Manueline style. Shelves soar over 20 metres around a vast reading room, crowned by a monumental stained-glass skylight that makes daylight part of the design.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-CA0206045106_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PortugueseLibrary_EN-CA0206045106_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Bookishly extravagant","Title":"Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Copyright":"© Antonio Salaverry/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-22.905431,-43.182116/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-22.905431,-43.182116;S9;Royal Portuguese Cabinet of Reading, Rio de Janeiro, Brazil&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Royal+Portuguese+Cabinet+of+Reading&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261024_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261024_PortugueseLibrary"},"Ssd":"20261024","Name":"PortugueseLibrary","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"0206045106","FullDateString":"Oct 24, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Two grey wolves move through the sagebrush of Yellowstone National Park in Wyoming, home to some of North America's most closely watched wolf packs. Their thick coats help them withstand harsh winters, and their keen senses make them skilled hunters and communicators.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-CA9692259331_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.YellowstoneWolves_EN-CA9692259331_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Partners in the wild","Title":"Two grey wolves Yellowstone National Park, Wyoming, United States","Copyright":"© John Morrison/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Grey wolves can communicate through howls, body language, scent marking and a range of vocalisations, including barks, whines and growls.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Wolf+Awareness+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261023_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261023_YellowstoneWolves"},"Ssd":"20261023","Name":"YellowstoneWolves","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9692259331","FullDateString":"Oct 23, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Few places in South Korea capture the magic of fall quite like Naejangsan National Park, where mountainsides glow in brilliant shades of scarlet, orange, yellow and gold. Located in the country's southwest, the park is particularly famous for its vivid maple colours, making it one of Korea's premier destinations for fall scenery. Its name, meaning 'many secrets in the mountains,' reflects the varied landscapes found throughout the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-CA9328142735_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NaejangsanNP_EN-CA9328142735_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Still waters, vivid colours","Title":"Fall in Naejangsan National Park, South Korea","Copyright":"© Twenty47studio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.481191,126.889374/3?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.481191,126.889374;S9;Naejangsan National Park, South Korea&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Naejangsan+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261022_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261022_NaejangsanNP"},"Ssd":"20261022","Name":"NaejangsanNP","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"9328142735","FullDateString":"Oct 22, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People paddle through flooded woodlands in Xuancheng, Anhui, where fall transforms bald cypress forests into a striking display of amber, copper and rust-coloured foliage. Unlike most conifers, bald cypress sheds its soft needles each fall after they turn reddish-brown. Native to North America, these trees thrive in wetlands, swamps and floodplains, often developing distinctive root \"knees\" that rise above the water. Some specimens have lived for more than 1,000 years. In late fall, the still water reflects the colourful canopy above, creating a remarkable landscape that highlights the bald cypress's natural connection to wetland environments.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-CA6102340228_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_EN-CA6102340228_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Paddling a painted forest","Title":"People rowing among colourful bald cypress, Xuancheng, Anhui, China","Copyright":"© Jackal Pan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/30.9525,118.75528/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=30.9525,118.75528;S9;Xuancheng, Anhui, China&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=bald+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261104_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina"},"Ssd":"20261104","Name":"AutumnChina","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"6102340228","FullDateString":"Nov 4, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lake Braies sits almost 1,500 metres above sea level in the Dolomites of South Tyrol, northern Italy. Surrounded by forest and the dramatic peaks of the Fanes-Sennes-Braies Nature Park, the lake is known for its striking green and blue waters. A 3.5-kilometre trail circles the shore, while traditional wooden rowing boats offer another way to take in the scenery. The lake is also a starting point for several mountain walks, including the Dolomites' famous Alta Via 1.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-CA5888574678_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_EN-CA5888574678_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Peace among the peaks","Title":"Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park, Dolomites, Italy","Copyright":"© leonid_tit/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/46.693566,12.084606/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=46.693566,12.084606;S9;Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Braies+Dolomites&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261103_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261103_AlpineBraies"},"Ssd":"20261103","Name":"AlpineBraies","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5888574678","FullDateString":"Nov 3, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"November marks an important time for polar bears along the shores of Hudson Bay in Manitoba, where they gather and wait for sea ice to form before returning to hunt seals. This annual event is celebrated during Polar Bear Week, observed in early November. Polar bears are powerful swimmers and highly adapted to Arctic life, but shrinking sea ice is forcing many to spend more time on land, making it harder to find food. The mother and cubs seen in today's image represent generations of bears that have followed this seasonal cycle, highlighting both the beauty of the Arctic and the importance of protecting the habitat these iconic Canadian animals depend on.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-CA5688581864_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_EN-CA5688581864_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A future written in ice","Title":"Polar bear and cubs by Hudson Bay, Manitoba, Canada","Copyright":"© Danita Delimont/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"In a single season, a polar bear may travel more than 1,000 kilometres in search of food and suitable sea ice.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Polar+Bear+Week&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261102_0500\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear"},"Ssd":"20261102","Name":"HudsonBear","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5688581864","FullDateString":"Nov 2, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Black Forest in south-west Germany is known for its misty landscapes, forested hills, deep valleys, lakes and picturesque towns. Stretching about 160 kilometres, the region is home to Feldberg, its highest peak at 1,493 metres, and marks the source of both the Danube and Neckar rivers. Beyond its natural beauty, the Black Forest is rich in history and tradition. Forestry has shaped the region for centuries, while its renowned clockmaking heritage helped make the cuckoo clock famous around the world. Today, the area remains one of Germany's most distinctive destinations, blending cultural heritage with striking scenery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-CA5505063549_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_EN-CA5505063549_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Mist among the trees","Title":"Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg, Germany","Copyright":"© Britus/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/48.286722,8.215281/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=48.286722,8.215281;S9;Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Black+Forest+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261101_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261101","Name":"SchwarzwaldAutumn","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5505063549","FullDateString":"Nov 1, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Frankfurt, Germany, provides a fitting backdrop for Halloween with St. Bartholomew's Cathedral and its striking Gothic tower. Yet the holiday's origins are even more intriguing. Many Halloween traditions are linked to Samhain, an ancient Celtic festival marking the end of the harvest season and the start of winter. People believed the boundary between the living and the dead grew thin, prompting bonfires, offerings and disguises to ward off wandering spirits. Later, the Christian observances of All Saints' Day and All Souls' Day helped shape Halloween as we know it today. St. Bartholomew's may set the scene, but Halloween brings the ghosts, legends and mystery.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-CA5228666040_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FrankfurtHalloween_EN-CA5228666040_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Ghosts of empires past","Title":"St. Bartholomew's Cathedral in Frankfurt, Germany","Copyright":"© AlxeyPnferov/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.110766,8.68539/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.110766,8.68539;S9;St. Bartholomew's Cathedral, Frankfurt, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261031_FrankfurtHalloween\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Halloween&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261031_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261031_FrankfurtHalloween"},"Ssd":"20261031","Name":"FrankfurtHalloween","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"5228666040","FullDateString":"Oct 31, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Winter transforms Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge in New Mexico into a haven for wildlife. Established in 1939, the 57,331-acre sanctuary provides an important stopover for migrating waterfowl and supports wildlife year-round. Sandhill cranes, featured in today's image, arrive in late October and spend the winter here, roosting in shallow water at night and feeding in nearby fields at sunrise. The refuge is a key wintering ground for the Rocky Mountain population of sandhill cranes. Other seasonal visitors include snow geese, northern pintails, hawks and eagles, while mule deer, coyotes and other mammals inhabit its diverse habitats.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-CA4395405990_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnCranes_EN-CA4395405990_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Time to fly high","Title":"Sandhill cranes, Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico, USA","Copyright":"© Terry St.Louis/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.384147,-106.900263/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.384147,-106.900263;S9;Bosque del Apache National Wildlife Refuge, New Mexico&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sandhill+Cranes&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261030_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261030_AutumnCranes"},"Ssd":"20261030","Name":"AutumnCranes","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"4395405990","FullDateString":"Oct 30, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As morning mist drifts among the standing stones of Avebury in Wiltshire, England, the scene feels almost timeless. These ancient megaliths form part of one of the world's most remarkable prehistoric landscapes, centred on a vast Neolithic monument built around 4,500 years ago. Avebury contains the world's largest prehistoric stone circle, as well as a massive henge and stone avenues extending into the surrounding countryside. Together with nearby monuments such as Silbury Hill and West Kennet Avenue, it forms part of an extensive Neolithic complex that has fascinated generations of visitors, researchers and archaeologists.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-CA3104504656_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AveburyStones_EN-CA3104504656_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where mist meets millennia","Title":"Standing stones at Avebury in Wiltshire, England","Copyright":"© George W Johnson/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.42898,-1.854909/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-CA&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.42898,-1.854909;S9;Avebury, Wiltshire, England&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Avebury+henge+Wiltshire&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261029_0400\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261029_AveburyStones"},"Ssd":"20261029","Name":"AveburyStones","Market":"EN-CA","Hash":"3104504656","FullDateString":"Oct 29, 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"Image